  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. Its first run finished with status `ok`, so the query runs without errors. It hasn't fired yet.\n\n**1. What the data holds:** The data view `Kibana Sample Data Logs` uses `timestamp` as its time field. Each document is one web request and includes:\n- the client (`clientip`, `agent`, `machine.os`)\n- the request (`url`, `request`, `extension`, `referer`, `host`)\n- the outcome (`response` as a string status code, and `bytes`)\n- geography (`geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `geo.coordinates`)\n\n**2. Dashboard \"EFF-541cf64b Web logs overview\":** 7 panels, defaulting to the last 7 days.\n- **Total requests:** count of requests.\n- **Unique visitors:** number of distinct `clientip` values.\n- **Total bytes served:** sum of `bytes`.\n- **Requests over time by response code:** bar chart over time, split by status code.\n- **Response code share:** pie chart.\n- **Top requested URLs:** table with request count and average bytes per URL.\n- **Top source countries:** bar chart of the top 10 `geo.src` values.\n\nLink: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-541cf64b-web-logs-overview-740bd7ab87ba\n\n**3. Rule \"EFF-541cf64b 5xx spike\"** (id `29cf3234-3161-4c91-9ae1-5ba1e6c90a91`):\n- It's an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs` that checks every minute.\n- It counts requests whose `response.keyword` is between `\"500\"` and `\"599\"`, using `timestamp`, over the last 5 minutes.\n- It fires when that count is more than 10.\n\n**Limitations:**\n- **API key was empty:** `KIBANA_TEST_API_KEY` was blank in the shell, so direct API calls returned 401. I did everything through the Kibana MCP tools instead, which meant I couldn't list the actual status code values.\n- **How the 5xx match works:** `response` is stored as text, not a number, so the 500\u2013599 range compares the codes as text. That matches correctly as long as every status code has exactly three digits, which is standard.\n- **No notifications:** the rule has no connector attached, so when it fires the alert only shows up in Kibana. Nothing is sent anywhere.",
